---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/prose.css';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Terms of Service — DevScrolls" 
  description="Terms of Service and Community Guidelines for DevScrolls, covering article discussions, accounts, developer tools, and content licenses."
>
  <div class="terms-container">
    <header class="terms-header">
      <h1 class="terms-title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="terms-subtitle">Last updated: September 20, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose terms-prose">
      <p class="lead">Welcome to DevScrolls (devscrolls.dev). By accessing our website, reading articles, utilizing developer tools, or participating in community discussions, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please discontinue use of the site.</p>

      <h2>1. User Accounts and Authentication</h2>
      <p>DevScrolls allows users to authenticate via third-party OAuth providers (Google and GitHub) to post comments, reply to discussions, and interact with community features.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality and security of the third-party accounts you use to log in.</li>
        <li>You agree to provide accurate information and not impersonate other individuals, engineers, or organizations.</li>
        <li>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate discussion access for any account found violating these terms or engaging in malicious activities.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Community Guidelines and Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>DevScrolls is a technical community dedicated to deep engineering discussions, frontend architecture, and practical software design. When posting comments or submitting feedback, you agree to adhere to the following rules:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Constructive Technical Discourse:</strong> Keep debates respectful and professional. Disagreement on architecture or technical trade-offs is welcome; personal attacks, harassment, discrimination, or abusive conduct are strictly prohibited.</li>
        <li><strong>No Spam or Unsolicited Promotion:</strong> Do not post affiliate links, unsolicited marketing, commercial advertisements, or link-farming comments.</li>
        <li><strong>No Malicious Content:</strong> Do not submit malicious payloads, executable scripts, exploit payloads, phishing links, or unauthorized code designed to compromise browsers or infrastructure.</li>
        <li><strong>Authentic Authorship:</strong> Do not post plagiarized content or material that infringes upon the intellectual property or copyright of others.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>DevScrolls reserves the right to review, edit, unpublish, or permanently delete any comment or discussion thread at its discretion without prior notice.</p>

      <h2>3. User-Generated Content License</h2>
      <p>When you submit comments, questions, or code snippets in DevScrolls discussion threads:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You retain ownership of any original intellectual property you create and submit.</li>
        <li>By posting on DevScrolls, you grant DevScrolls a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free, perpetual license to host, display, format, and distribute your content across the site in connection with article discussions.</li>
        <li>You can delete your comments directly from the discussion section at any time while signed into the account used to create them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Developer Tools and Educational Content</h2>
      <p>All articles, architecture breakdowns, code examples, and browser-based developer utilities (including JSON Formatter, DailyScroll, and related tools) are provided strictly for educational and informational purposes.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>"As-Is" Availability:</strong> The tools and code snippets are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis, without express or implied warranties of any kind.</li>
        <li><strong>Client-Side Processing:</strong> Unless explicitly noted, developer utilities process data entirely within your local browser sandbox. However, you are solely responsible for validating output before running code or loading sensitive production data.</li>
        <li><strong>No Professional Liability:</strong> DevScrolls and its authors are not liable for system outages, data loss, security bugs, or technical failures resulting from the implementation of architectural advice or code published on this site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Job Board and External Links</h2>
      <p>DevScrolls features an aggregated engineering job board and links to third-party repositories, documentation, and external platforms:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Job listings and application links direct you to external third-party ATS platforms or hiring companies. DevScrolls is not an employer, recruiter, or staffing agency for aggregated roles.</li>
        <li>We make reasonable efforts to filter legitimate listings, but we do not guarantee employment, salary accuracy, or company verification.</li>
        <li>We are not responsible for the content, privacy practices, or availability of third-party websites linked across our platform.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
      <p>Except for user-submitted comments and open-source packages licensed under respective permissive licenses, all original articles, editorial text, custom graphics, illustrations, and site source code on DevScrolls are the intellectual property of DevScrolls and protected by applicable copyright laws. Reproduction, redistribution, or mirroring without prior written permission is prohibited.</p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, DevScrolls, its maintainers, contributors, and affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your access to or use of, or inability to access or use, the website or services.</p>

      <h2>8. Modifications to Terms</h2>
      <p>We reserve the right to revise these Terms of Service at any time. Changes will be effective immediately upon posting to this page, with the revision date noted at the top. Your continued use of the website following changes indicates your acceptance of the updated terms.</p>

      <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions, feedback, or concerns regarding these Terms of Service, contact us at <a href="mailto:santhanakrishnanstark@gmail.com">santhanakrishnanstark@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms-container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .terms-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .terms-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .terms-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .terms-prose {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
</style>
